      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T22:37:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible that the fallback connection comes with no profile connected?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 941,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 941,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "7ad7b0ca2ecb6591f85e1161577037ca9a541f52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11e33a51_c175148d",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 941,
      "author": {
        "id": 1957996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-07T11:00:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fallback connection (which is a task stored in |self.device_added_tasks|) is not meant to be run when no profile is connected (i.e., when the last update was a remove event that cleared |self.connected_profiles|), and could only run when there was ever a successful profile connection.\n\nNote how \"once there is a moment all profiles get cleared\", we try to reset all the states (see |is_profile_cleared|).\n\nThe change in aosp/2321211 makes this a little bit more tricky... there is some chance where the task could be aborted (due to cleared profiles after |ACCEPTOR_CONNECT_MISSING_PROFILES_TIMEOUT_SEC|) between |MediaActions::Connect| and the fallback connections, but in that case we have been through the reset, so whatever missing profiles are being connected to won\u0027t cause much issue and we can catch up at the fallback connection following that one.\n\nThese are the ideal cases and I could be missing something around, feel free to disagree about any part and we can work on a less complicated architecture (i.e., start building some strong assumptions).",
      "parentUuid": "8c90d9fd_c0df073a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 941,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 941,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "7ad7b0ca2ecb6591f85e1161577037ca9a541f52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fbb5225_598d287b",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 941,
