        "id": 1543626
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-07T23:08:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the clarification of the none profile connected case.\n\nSome points I\u0027d like to highlight regarding the profile connection:\n1. Bluetooth stack should have all profile connected before telling Audio stack that the device is ready. (This is not true now as a temporal mitigation that we should start to fix.)\n2. We should collect these race sequence and refine the codes regardingly. As you described, aosp/2321211 mitigates the issue but brings more complexity to the profile connection flow.\n\nI\u0027m fine with this patch, but I\u0027ll suggest to add a TODO to refine reconnect logic brought by aosp/2321211. \n\nMy rough idea is to generalize it to a flow like:\n1. Host or HF side trigger the profile connected event.\n2. Check if all of the profiles are ready, notify audio stack if yes. If not, trigger missing profile connection and schedule a task to check again\n3. Repeat 2. until we hit a retry limit or time limit.\n\nI think we\u0027ll still need to handle the random disconnection event in the run, but we\u0027ll have a easier to improve state-machine flow.",
      "parentUuid": "11e33a51_c175148d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 941,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 941,
        "endChar": 46
      },
